Well I agree that anyway typing ^^7f is not a possibility, but unless
I misunderstand what you mean, even catcode 11 would not help. The
^^7f glyph in the new dc fonts is not suitable as a compound word
mark, with any catcode. It has to come at the end of a line it may not
be used mid-line as it sticks out on the right.

However all this discussion is clarifying what the *current* position
is. Probably a more useful discusion is to discuss what functionality
people need for various languages, and how that might be declared...

